  "brief_notes": "Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead in this session). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\n\n- The feature was motivated by the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22. There, every review round re-ran a 72-check matrix of about 35 minutes, and intermittent suites failed roughly one run in three.\n- In this repository `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so `--carry` saves little here. The dogfood record at c4182727 carried five of six modules with zero changed files.\n- Please challenge the soundness argument of D1 in particular. A carried result is bound to the material computed at HEAD, and that is only safe when the selection guarantees the carried module's inputs did not change.\n- Please also check the derived-record exclusion (`carryExclusions` with `posemodel.IsAdministrativePath`) and the engine identity, which is the version plus the VCS revision.\n- Report every finding you see in this round, each classified as blocker or follow-up.\n",
